{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","kind":"proposition","title":"Third-generation meson ($\\phi$) mass ratio from Hecke characters and Seifert volumes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-meson","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hoefsmit-binding-amplitude","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/kassel1995"],"tags":["meson","phi","pion","hecke-character","seifert-volume","torus-knot","mass-ratio","third-generation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Mass.Gen3.phiMassRatio","text":"gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.md","leanSource":"gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert\"></a><p><em>The third-generation meson built on the torus knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,7)</code> has mass ratio:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\frac{\\mathfrak{m}_X}{\\mathfrak{m}_\\pi}\n  \\;=\\; \\chi^{(2,1)}(\\sigma_1^7)\\cdot\\Bigl(\\frac{V_S(T(2,7))}{V_S(T(2,3))}\\Bigr)^2.</code></pre>\n<p>Its value at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> and the identification with a measured meson are recorded in <a href=\"#rem:gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert-identification\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-physical-face\">this remark</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.37.9","page":"b/prop-gen3-meson-phi-hecke-seifert","qa":{"counts":{"pass":84,"fail":2,"warn":3,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassin